filter-env oracle case: edge-empty

Isolates the empty input: real copies nothing, exits 0, writes no
stdout and no stderr. It pins the trivial edge of the read loop.
If the native port regressed to erroring on empty input, rc.txt
would be nonzero or stderr.txt non-empty.

Run exactly as the phase runtime runs it:
  /usr/bin/python <checkout>/bin/filter-bash-environment.py "$(cat args)" < in > out 2> stderr.txt
Byte-exact: the args file bytes are argv[1] (no trailing newline
added, none present); the in file bytes are stdin verbatim.

Provenance (D4):
  portage-ref: portage-3.0.82.2
  portage-commit: 1d95fc2c552a2c7d347e54093fa0e5b172a57004 (3rdparty/repos.toml [portage] commit)
  python: Python 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python)
  input: hand-written (see the case name); args is the captured
    install-phase pattern (2378 bytes) except edge-pattern-metachars
    (its own minimal real-caller-vocabulary pattern) and
    error-bad-pattern (the single byte `(`).
  sizes: args=2378 in=0 out=0
  date: 2026-10-08 (UTC day granularity; the only field that may change
    between regenerations)
